  "subtitle": "Capture conference agenda, student work, attendance context, and family question; confirm agreed action and progress follow-up.",
  "description": "Parent Conference records conference agenda, student work, attendance context, family question, agreed action, and progress follow-up. Parent Conference evidence stays linked.",
  "use_case": "Use this parent conference evidence-based review when staff must document conference agenda and student work. Reconcile attendance context, family question, agreed action, and progress follow-up before the parent conference handoff. Use the conference invitation, work samples, gradebook snapshot, attendance record, teacher observations, family questions, action notes, and progress-review calendar. For parent conference review use, cite source. Match the parent conference family or learner wording. Preserve the parent conference amendment history and supersession date. Link the parent conference source version and meeting notes. Record the parent conference learner response and accessibility support. Close the parent conference recipient list. Verify parent conference documentary provenance. Resolve parent conference amendments, superseded wording, and archival distribution for parent conference. Ask the assigned parent conference reviewer to confirm conference agenda against the organization's policy.",
  "risk_tier": "B",
